  "question": {
    "text": "Let <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>y</mi><mo>=</mo><mi>y</mi><mfenced><mi>x</mi></mfenced></math> be the solution of the differential equation <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>x</mi><mo>&#160;</mo><mi>tan</mi><mfenced><mfrac><mi>y</mi><mi>x</mi></mfrac></mfenced><mi>d</mi><mi>y</mi><mo>=</mo><mfenced><mrow><mi>y</mi><mo>&#160;</mo><mi>tan</mi><mfenced><mfrac><mi>y</mi><mi>x</mi></mfrac></mfenced><mo>-</mo><mi>x</mi></mrow></mfenced><mi>d</mi><mi>x</mi></math>,&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mo>-</mo><mn>1</mn><mo>&#8804;</mo><mi>x</mi><mo>&#8804;</mo><mn>1</mn><mo>,</mo><mi>y</mi><mfenced><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mn>2</mn></mfrac></mfenced><mo>=</mo><mfrac><mi>&#960;</mi><mn>6</mn></mfrac><mo>.</mo></math> Then the area of the region bounded by the curves <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>x</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>0</mn><mo>,</mo><mi>x</mi><mo>=</mo><mfrac><mn>1</mn><msqrt><mn>2</mn></msqrt></mfrac></math> and <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>y</mi><mo>=</mo><mi>y</mi><mfenced><mi>x</mi></mfenced></math>&nbsp;in the upper half plane is:"
  },
